{
  "name": "vector_light_door_close",
  "saveFile": "minimal_colony.rws",
  "description": "Issue #174 phase 1, filmed: does the beam track a door's leaves on the way SHUT the way \u00a727e phase 2 taught it to on the way open. Two hand-rolled sweeps over the same wooden door's close, differing only in vector_light_door_aperture. Hand-rolled rather than TickLapse for the reason phase 2 records -- AdvanceTicks is a jump, so a door's own Tick() never runs under it and a film of nothing passes; SetTimeSpeed normal is what makes the leaves move. The number the fix rests on is door_aperture_bakes over the close: nine, the same nine an open costs, where the code this replaces saw the aperture read 0 on the first tick of the slide, baked once and drained. The flag-off arm is the behaviour being replaced rather than the feature being absent -- with no aperture the cell is a whole-cell occluder from the tick openInt goes false, which is exactly what the old code did with the flag on. Composition flags are stated rather than inherited: this measures WHEN the geometry moves, and phase 6's per-fragment max would move the level of every frame without touching the timing under test.",
